[h1]D'thorga Patches[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.43.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published yet - draft held for the owner's review

[h2]Read this first (gotchas)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Partly tested in game:[/b] putting out stuck vehicle fires, one missile strike on an earlier version, the Prison Labor guard, drone platforms kept topped up and drones called home in time, soldiers going back to their own guns, sidearms that loop being stopped, mech rechargers drawing real power, and the Nice Research Tab guard. Everything else is [b]not yet tested in game[/b].
[*][b]Needs Harmony and D'thorga Framework (0.184.0 or later).[/b] [b]Load it after the mods it patches[/b]; the mod asks for that order itself, so RimSort sorts it for you. [b]Switch it on yourself[/b]: nothing else requires it. [b]RimWorld 1.7 only.[/b]
[*][b]Each part loads only while its own mods are active.[/b] A player running none of them sees nothing.
[*][b]It replaces D'thorga Vehicle Patches and D'thorga Missile Patches:[/b] switch both off and this one on in the same change.
[*][b]Safe to add to a running colony.[/b] A Harrier, A-10 or Su-25 you already built keeps working and gains its new parts at full health; only new builds pay the new cost. Finish or cancel a Harrier, Black Hawk or C-17 frame before installing.
[*][b]Before removing it:[/b] delete any bomb, rocket or heavy casting bills you added; [b]with Combat Extended, use up or sell your bomb cases, bomb fills and missile seeker heads[/b], and deconstruct turret hulls built under this mod (not yet tested either way).
[*][b]Missile strikes:[/b] decide the blast settings before a strike; choices that cost speed say so. [b]After a strike, wait for the message that the blast has spent itself before saving.[/b]
[*][b]With Biotech, mech rechargers drawing real power is off by default.[/b] Before turning it on, check your grid: a tunneler or war queen charging draws about 1,000 W or more.
[*][b]The Harrier cannot be taken apart yet.[/b] Try one disassembly only on a copy of your save, and stop there.
[*][b]Close Air Support's Realistic handling is off by default.[/b] On, the A-10 and Su-25 fly at speeds set by the real aircraft's against the Harrier's.
[*][b]Rearming keeps to one kind of ammunition[/b] (Harrier, Hind, Mongoose, A-10, Su-25). To change kind, choose it on the weapon.
[*][b]Combat Extended:[/b] allow the two bomb cases in machining bay hoppers that used to take heavy castings, and rebuild turret hulls built before, while the ship is landed. Soldiers go back to their own guns after being downed (on by default); a colonist who already has no gun needs one handed to them once.
[*][b]With RimPacts, a world war attack must win within 3 days of accepting it[/b], or about a dozen border towns pass to the enemy. That is RimPacts' own rule; the quest now shows the countdown.
[*][b]With Visit Settlements, pawns already lost to a closed map stay lost:[/b] load a save from before.
[/list]

[h2]What it does[/h2]
Fixes and patches for other authors' mods, each switched on only while that mod is active. It copies nothing from them.
[list]
[*][b]Harrier VTOL Attack Aircraft:[/b] built from real parts by role (a turbine, four nozzles, landing gear, fuel tanks, electrics, hydraulics, avionics), with flight controls that ground the jet when damaged. It now loads fully beside RimPacts, and a sortie's map stays open while the jet flies over it.
[*][b]UH-60M Black Hawk[/b], [b]C-17 Globemaster III[/b] and [b]Close Air Support: A-10 Warthog & Su-25 Frogfoot:[/b] built from real parts by role.
[*][b]Combat Extended and The Dead Man's Switch:[/b] bombs whose ingredients match what they weigh, each on a stackable steel bomb case; bombs and rockets at the ammunition fabricator; RimThunder's heavy castings 12 at a time at the rotary forger; drone platforms refilled by colonists, drones called home in time and their wrecks carried back.
[*][b]Spaceship Turret Hull:[/b] the armed hulls load and fire Combat Extended ammunition like any other turret.
[*][b]InterRim Ballistic Missile:[/b] a strategic warhead no longer freezes the game. The blast crosses the map a slice at a time and ends in seconds; overhead mountain shelters what is under it. The extinction-class warhead strikes with a fireball, a blast zone and a heat zone, with Dubs Rimatomics' fallout where it is active.
[*][b]Biotech[/b] (a setting, off by default): mech rechargers draw power by the size of the mech on them.
[*][b]Vanilla Factions Expanded - Classical:[/b] a save made during a scorpion raid loads with the raid still working.
[*][b]Nice Research Tab:[/b] a blank entry can no longer stop the research tab opening.
[*][b]Vehicle Framework:[/b] fires a vehicle could never put out are put out, and a vehicle saved mid-burst keeps itself, its crew and its cargo. With Vanilla Expanded Framework, a caravan with vehicles cannot found an outpost and lose them.
[*][b]Visit Settlements:[/b] a visited settlement's map stays open while your people can still act there.
[/list]

Settings are in Options > Mod settings > D'thorga Patches, a page for each patched mod. How each part works is in the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-rimworld/blob/main/docs/player-guide/patches.md]player guide's Patches chapter[/url].

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.7
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]
[*]D'thorga Framework, 0.184.0 or later
[/list]
It does nothing unless at least one of the mods it patches is active.

